// Galata Tower, Istanbul, over a street of colourful buildings. A portal has torn open in the sky above the tower.
// The buildings (near.png) are traced from a photo with `cargo run --bin trace_photo`; the sky, the portal and the
// cobbles come from `cargo run --bin gen_sprites`. Swap any image for your own art.
// Layers go back to front. parallax: 1 = fixed on screen, 0 = fixed in the world. glow: true makes a layer pulse (the portal).
(
    name: "Galata Tower",
    sky: (0.50, 0.76, 0.98),
    pillar: (0.62, 0.72, 0.88),
    floor_a: (0.58, 0.52, 0.52),
    floor_b: (0.50, 0.45, 0.46),
    layers: [
        (image: "backgrounds/galata/sky.png", parallax: 1.0, z: -10.0),
        (image: "backgrounds/galata/portal.png", parallax: 0.0, z: -7.5, glow: true),
        (image: "backgrounds/galata/near.png", parallax: 0.0, z: -8.0),
    ],
    floor_tile: Some("backgrounds/galata/floor.png"),
)
